===Golden Skin Strategies===
*'''For the first task''', play normally until you find {{CI|Twisted Bobette|name=true}}, get in her sight, then try to find her again in another [[Floor]]. It should be noted that you'll likely have better luck when she is on the [[Daily Twisted Board]]. You could also go in a run and aim for [[Floor]] 20, as it guarantees a Twisted Bobette spawn, and will also help with the '''second task'''. You can even go on a solo run since her survivability is quite high.
*'''For the second task''', join a run and try to aim for Floor 20. You should pair {{TI|Magnifying Glass|name=true}} or {{TI|Vee's Remote|name=true}} alongside {{TI|Toy Kit|name=true}} for faster Floor progression. If there is a 2 {{Star}} [[Stealth]] distractor, you can use {{TI|Diary|name=true}} to solar distract with the distractor.
*'''For the final task''', try to avoid voting {{CDI|Frost Shield|name=true}} and try to vote {{CDI|Piping Tape|name=true}} and {{CDI|Electrician|name=true}} instead, as it will enhance the chances of the Iced Over Floor Event happening. This task is best done during long runs.

==Strategies==
Bobette is a great all-rounder [[Toon]] due to her jack-of-all-trades kit. Her Active [[Ability]], {{AI|Bobette}}'''Precious Packaging''', can be extremely helpful in sticky situations, such as being chased by a {{Type|Lethal}} or [[:Category:Ranged Twisteds|Ranged]] [[Twisted]]. Unlike {{CI|Connie|name=true}}'s Ability and {{II|Smoke Bomb}}[[Items|Smoke Bombs]], Bobette's Ability is able to save her from the aforementioned Twisteds, which makes her a great pick for those who prefer to be survivalists. It should be noted that a Twisted may come to your location while you are still in the box, so you must be careful. It's usually safer to use this Ability around corners or against walls because of how Twisteds behave. This is because most do not stall, so they will either move forward or go the other way. Twisteds stop at predetermined locations, so knowledge of their pathing is helpful if you want to play her. The cooldown of her Active Ability won't start counting down until she stops hiding in the present, unless she is under the effects of {{Debuff|Ignited}}.

In runs with multiple people or distractors, Bobette's Active Ability also allows her to assist distractors if they lose sight of any Twisteds by bringing them back to the distractor and using her Ability to force Twisteds to go after the distractor instead. When using this strategy, try to brush against their looping zone without being so close that you steal aggro immediately again. In certain cases, the distractor will be able to retrieve them themselves if they have an {{II|Air Horn|name=true}}, are playing {{CI|Pebble|name=true}} and use his {{AI|Pebble}}'''Speak!''' Ability, or if they are using {{TI|Scrapbook|name=true}} and their [[Stealth]] is equal or below 2 Stars, so if the above are the case, it's best to save her Ability than to use it immediately.

Bobette is beneficial to have when it comes to many things. Her 4{{Star}} [[Skill Check]] [[Stat]] allows her to be a decent extractor (especially with {{TI|Magnifying Glass|name=true}}/{{TI|Participation Award|name=true}}), however her 2 Star [[Extraction Speed]] may hinder this, making her extraction stats the exact same as {{CI|Tisha|name=true}}'s. Her Mobility is above average with 5 Stars in [[Stamina]] and a 3 Stars in [[Movement Speed]], allowing her to escape Twisteds easily. Her great mobility [[Statistics]], alongside her above average Skill Check, make her a great Toon to extract [[Treadmill Machines]] with. It may be beneficial to help someone on a Treadmill Machine, as the Movement Speed and Stamina boost from her Passive Ability can help finish the Machine faster. This is especially applicable for Duo Machines, as Bobette is already quite capable at extracting all Machine types anyways, being able to support whoever is working with her, if they're on a treadmill attachment.

Despite having 2 Star [[Stealth]], Bobette can be a very good solo Toon. She has the survivability and the (somewhat) good extraction to make it far in the right hands, although she does require some caution, given her status as a [[Main Character]] decreasing her heart count and her below-average Stealth equal to some Toons like {{CI|Vee|name=true}} and {{CI|Glisten|name=true}}.

Bobette's '''Festive Aura''' grants a decent stamina regeneration source, as well as a good enough speed boost to escape Twisteds. It works like a combination of a {{II|Stamina Candy|name=false}} and {{II|Speed Candy|name=false}}, making Bobette a good Toon to help teammates get away from danger. Her only conflict with her Passive is her lower Stealth, but this can also be used to your advantage to take aggro from chasing Twisteds, giving your teammate a better chance to escape. When the Elevator opens at the start of a Floor, you can run in a small circle, or back and forth to give the entire team a speed boost. If you're inside the Elevator during [[Panic Mode]], you can still help your team by standing on the edge (behind the inner yellow line), as the aura is big enough to stick outside of the Elevator. Both of these applications are easier to do if you equip {{TI|Toy Kit|name=true}}, for you and your teammates.

Bobette's '''Festive Aura''' can be used to help 2 Star Stealth distractors distract faster Twisteds with ease, like {{CI|Twisted Pebble|name=true}}. If a {{CI|Looey|name=true}}, {{CI|Eclipse|name=true}}, or {{CI|Goob|name=true}} intends to distract {{CI|Twisted Dyle|name=true}} with the help of Items, she can also use her Passive Ability to give them a speed boost. The above scenarios will only work if Bobette is using {{TI|Diary|name=true}}, or the distractor is using {{TI|Scrapbook|name=true}}. In either case, this allows Bobette to perform a strategy called solar system kiting, where the distractor goes clockwise or counterclockwise and Bobette circles the opposite direction, giving the distractor a consistent 25% speed boost and 50% stamina regeneration. Caution will need to be taken while doing this strategy, as the distractor needs to be careful to not take sharp corners to prevent Twisteds from aggroing on Bobette.

When it comes to Items, those related with Stamina such as {{II|Protein Bar|name=false|plural=a}} or {{II|Pop|name=false}} are very helpful. Bobette's 5 Star Stamina can take a while to fully regenerate, and her 3 Star Movement Speed means she needs to run quite often, thus having Stamina Items on hand will allow her to take full advantage of her mobility. {{II|Jumper Cable|name=false|plural=a}}, {{II|Skill Check Candy|name=false|plural=a}}, {{II|Instructions|name=false}}, and {{II|Valve|name=false|plural=a}} are good extraction Items that can remedy Bobette's lower Extraction Speed or support her proficiency with Skill Checks. Since she is a Main Character, it's recommended to prioritize {{II|Bandage|name=false|plural=a}} due to them healing one Heart, avoiding any wastage. If you're solar kiting with a distractor, having at least one healing Item is strongly recommended due to the potential danger you're vulnerable to. Mobility Items can also help you keep up with your distractor, especially during Panic Mode.

Overall Bobette is quite capable at practically anything. Extracting, surviving, scouting, supporting, and protecting are all tasks she can effectively fulfill. It's a good idea to choose [[Trinkets]] that primarily hone in on one task you wish you do, allowing Bobette to be more effective in that area. However, two separate Trinkets (such as a mobility and extraction Trinket) for different tasks can also be utilized to enhance a generalist playstyle, if that is what you are seeking with her instead.

